# Copy to backend/.env and fill in, or run ./scripts/init-env.sh, which copies this file. Tags:
#   REQUIRED  — uncommented; the agent refuses to start without it, naming the key.
#   OPTIONAL  — commented out at its default, or at an example when it has none; uncomment to set.
#   TEST-ONLY — commented out; leave unset, the tests set it.
# The scripts export this file and compose passes it to the containers. A variable already exported
# in the calling shell wins over the same key here, and a blank value counts as unset.

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — matches the bundled docker-compose database (published on 127.0.0.1:5434).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://hfm:hfm@localhost:5434/hfm

# ── Language model (writes the report narrative; numbers never come from it) ─────
# REQUIRED — provider:model, anthropic or openai. The model only phrases totals computed in
# code, so the cheapest tier does; anthropic:claude-haiku-5-5 is the Anthropic equivalent. A GPT-5
# model is asked for minimal reasoning effort, since on its default a few sentences can take over a
# minute.
LLM_MODEL=openai:gpt-5-nano
# REQUIRED — the API key of the provider LLM_MODEL names.
LLM_API_KEY=
# OPTIONAL — how many days a written report keeps answering for the same totals instead of the
# model; a person's older reports are forgotten when their next one is written.
# REPORT_MEMORY_RETENTION_DAYS=90
# TEST-ONLY — docker-compose.e2e.yml sets it so the end-to-end test shows a canned report and
# reads neither LLM_MODEL nor LLM_API_KEY.
# HFM_E2E=true

# ── Sign in with Google ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — the OAuth client id of this agent's Google Cloud project (type "Web application",
# authorized JavaScript origin http://localhost:8010). The page signs people in with it, and
# every token the API accepts must be issued to it. docs/sign-in.md walks through the setup.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# OPTIONAL — who issues the tokens and where their public keys are published; Google's by
# default. docker-compose.e2e.yml points the issuer at a test issuer.
# AUTH_ISSUER=https://accounts.google.com
# AUTH_JWKS_URL=https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v3/certs
# TEST-ONLY — a PEM public key that replaces AUTH_JWKS_URL, so tests sign their own tokens.
# AUTH_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE=

# ── Card agents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — the registry of connected card agents, written by ./scripts/add-card-agent.sh and read
# at startup; docs/architecture/configuration.md describes its entries. Absent or empty, no card
# agent is connected and the page says so. Default: beside this file; compose mounts it at
# /card-agents.yaml.
# CARD_AGENTS_FILE=backend/card-agents.yaml

# ── Config files and the page ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — the monthly budget; a relative path resolves against the agent's working directory
# (the repo root in start.sh --host, /app in the image).
# BUDGET_CONFIG=config/budget.yaml
# OPTIONAL — folder of the built React page, served at /; unset (the default) serves the API only.
# start.sh --host and the image set it.
# HFM_FRONTEND_DIST=frontend/dist

# ── Live events ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — a Redis URL (redis://[:password@]host:port/db) that carries live review events
# between replicas of this agent, so a browser's event stream may be served by a replica other
# than the one running the review. Unset, events stay inside the one process. Compose sets it to
# its redis service; a single start.sh --host process needs none.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# ── Checkpoints ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — LangGraph's checkpoint serializer is permissive by default (false); true blocks any
# value type outside the review's allow-list, logging a warning instead of restoring it. start.sh,
# compose and the tests set it to true, so it needs no value here.
# LANGGRAPH_STRICT_MSGPACK=true

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — root log level, and per-module overrides (none by default; the example shows the
# shape).
# HFM_LOG_LEVEL=WARNING
# HFM_LOG_LEVELS=hfm.application.review_graph=DEBUG
